From ad84c18898beee7b854fa3cc64829dd26414cbce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 22:07:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][GBM][GLES] SDR in a wide container: DCI-P3 (D65)
 besides BT.2020

The composite of the GUI into SDR of BT.2020 primaries, the conversion of
Kodi's shaders and the colorimetry told to the display knew BT.2020 only.
HDR mapped to SDR for a projector or a TV that takes DCI-P3 needs the same
in DCI-P3 with the white of D65 (SMPTE EG 432-1).

- SdrWide.h: a container (BT.709, BT.2020, DCI-P3 (D65)), its matrix (BT.709
  to DCI-P3 in linear light, made from the CIE xy as BT.2087's is), the GUI
  converted into it, and why one is not used: the EDID and the connector are
  asked for the value of that container.
- gles_gui_composite.frag: u_sdrWide 2.0 converts the GUI into DCI-P3 by the
  same ITU-R BT.2087 case #1 conversion; 1.0 is BT.2020 as before.
- CGuiCompositeShaderGLES::SDR_P3_D65, GetSdrContainer().
- CConvertMatrix: DCI-P3 (D65) as a destination, with the 2.4 of BT.2020's
  SDR signal; a source of those primaries is taken as before.
- CDisplayInfo: DCI-P3 RGB is the bit that CTA-861-H names SMPTE ST 2113 RGB
  (libdisplay-info's st2113_rgb).
- CWinSystemGbm: DisplayDeclaresP3Rgb(), ConnectorOffersP3Rgb(),
  SetColorimetryP3D65(); SetColorimetry() sets the property through
  ApplyColorimetry(), unchanged.

Nothing calls the DCI-P3 container yet: SDR videos of BT.2020 go out as
before.
